[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3 uid="uid://unitsprite3dnestmod"]

; ONE VARIABLE: what a Sprite3D's PARENT contributes to its drawn colour —
; `SpriteBase3D::_get_color_accum()` (`scene/3d/sprite_3d.cpp:36-52`).
;
; The accumulation walks the IMMEDIATE parent only (`:75` casts `get_parent()`
; to SpriteBase3D and stops), so it is a no-op in every other scene in the
; corpus: a Sprite3D parented to a Node3D accumulates from white and draws
; exactly its own modulate, which is what a renderer that ignores the rule
; entirely also draws. A regression is therefore invisible anywhere a sprite is
; not directly nested under another sprite, and nothing else nests them.
;
; All four columns carry the SAME child modulate. The leftmost is the control
; and shows it unaccumulated; only the second may differ from it. Columns three
; and four re-run the second through an intervening Node3D and an intervening
; Label3D — Label3D derives from GeometryInstance3D (`label_3d.h:38`) exactly
; as SpriteBase3D does (`sprite_3d.h:36`), so it is a sibling, not an ancestor,
; and breaks the chain despite carrying a `modulate` of its own.
;
; The two modulates differ in every channel and in alpha, and neither equals
; the product, so an RGB-only accumulation and a skipped one both read as a
; different picture rather than a subtler one.

